e of each on 4.<br /> <br /> Not sure if it was different before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:28:50-07:00","id":1301997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1301984#post1301984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prety sure it\u2019s the rule. You start with 2 Booms and 4 Callings, gais a calling in legend 2, 1 boom on 3, one of each on 4.<br /> <br /> Not sure if it was different before.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you\u2019re supposed to have Legend + 1 Boon slots consistently. In the preview text they forgot the \u201c+1\u201d, and it appears they only fixed it for Legend 1 in the new text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-02-2019, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:54:41-07:00","id":1302032,"title":"","content":"Yep... and my perfect printed copy will have these glaring errors in it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:17:53-07:00","id":1302036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1302032#post1302032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep... and my perfect printed copy will have these glaring errors in it</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you seeing this confirmed? Last I saw Neall was looking into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:00:04-07:00","id":1302081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1302036#post1302036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are you seeing this confirmed? Last I saw Neall was looking into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>MMN: <br /> Scion Hero \u2013 Shipping from printer to fulfillment shipper this week.<br /> Scion Origin \u2013 Shipping from printer to fulfillment shipper this week.<br /> <br /> Aka... book is printed and now shipping to the crew who ships it to us. If we were given that text.. as the final pdf. It stands to reason that OP are printing that text. So basically. Congratulations and welcome to a printed copy of that text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:23:03-07:00","id":1302089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1302081#post1302081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MMN: <br /> Scion Hero*\u2013*Shipping from printer to fulfillment shipper this week.<br /> Scion Origin \u2013*Shipping from printer to fulfillment shipper this week.<br /> <br /> Aka... book is printed and now shipping to the crew who ships it to us. If we were given that text.. as the final pdf. It stands to reason that OP are printing that text. So basically. Congratulations and welcome to a printed copy of that text.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hope is that the file they uploaded is not the file that was sent to the printers. We are waiting for confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T21:05:01-07:00","id":1302107,"title":"","content":"What's got me worried is there is a ton of things that were reported several times during the backers previews and during the development that never was addressed or fixed. Purviews that don't exist but still are on some of the god list, god's not updated to the correct callings and purviews in origin, the fact that they're still not existed, modified paths in origin their hinted on page 167. A lot of these have been addressed or commented on several times by backers but looks like it was forgotten","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T23:21:59-07:00","id":1302127,"title":"","content":"So Rich said today on Monday Meeting Notes...<br /> <br /> &quot;I haven\u2019t notified backers in an Update yet, as I need to also set up the PoD coupons, but the final PDFs are already up today. You can download the updated ones in your DTRPG library. If you\u2019re not a backer, Scion will be available to the public on DTRPG around the same time as stores will have the physical books.&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words. We have the final draft. So either we're going to get pages of eratta ot we're going to get nothing fixed. I wonder if anyone even read the eratta thread...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T23:53:34-07:00","id":1302132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1302127#post1302127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Rich said today on Monday Meeting Notes...<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;I haven\u2019t notified backers in an Update yet, as I need to also set up the PoD coupons, but the final PDFs are already up today. You can download the updated ones in your DTRPG library. If you\u2019re not a backer, Scion will be available to the public on DTRPG around the same time as stores will have the physical books.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In other words. We have the final draft. So either we're going to get pages of eratta ot we're going to get nothing fixed. I wonder if anyone even read the eratta thread...</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been uploaded file mix ups before. Neall is looking into why several things that were fixed aren\u2019t fixed in this pdf and what got sent to the printer. There is no reason not to wait to hear his answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T13:39:09-07:00","id":1302319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1302132#post1302132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There have been uploaded file mix ups before. Neall is looking into why several things that were fixed aren\u2019t fixed in this pdf and what got sent to the printer. There is no reason not to wait to hear his answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on that, Neall knows about some of the errors and commented that he distinctly remembers correcting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T20:28:36-07:00","id":1302429,"title":"","content":"I honestly would not bet on the \u201cWrong Upload\u201d. Most of the problems are on the way it is written and contradictions between pages on the same subject. <br /> There is a few formatting mistakes, much less than the backers preview, but still some. Some game terms that were removed are still present, like Saints being called godly or something like that...<br /> <br /> My opinion didn\u2019t change about the way the 2 books don\u2019t work fine together, Hero have too many text that is in Origin, Heroic Knacks, description of the denizens, some qualities. I do like the idea of one book to rule than all, but Hero doesn\u2019t, neither does Origin, so they could focus on what\u2019s new and not copy paste of so many texts. Copying text could cause contraditiction as one is corrected and the other no (as it happened to Kitsune and some of the permanent conditions of the denizens).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s annoying go thru 3 books as we needed to do to build a god (or even a Hero with some exotic knacks) on 1e, but it\u2019s the best way to keep the books working fine together.<br /> <br /> Now the good part, I liked a lot the new arts, the 2 old Shen and the young one playing risk made me laugh more than I would like to admit, not a big deal, but... The new \u201cstandardised\u201d experience cost make the use of Edges and skill tricks possible, as it really annoyed me they are not available, Origin and Heroes need the more human side to be ready...<br /> <br /> The way they described the scales is much much much more clear than before, and Tiers are described apart of it, making it clear that they are not the same thing. I didn\u2019t read thru everything, actually Inwent straight to the points that were not clear before, so many thing that were clear in my mind (it doesn\u2019t mean it was working before, just that I had a proper image of it)...<br /> In the next few days I intend to go thru Origin properly, and latter Hero... until there I will go easy on the critics...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T21:43:48-07:00","id":1302458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1302429#post1302429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly would not bet on the \u201cWrong Upload\u201d. Most of the problems are on the way it is written and contradictions between pages on the same subject.<br /> There is a few formatting mistakes, much less than the backers preview, but still some. Some game terms that were removed are still present, like Saints being called godly or something like that...<br /> <br /> My opinion didn\u2019t change about the way the 2 books don\u2019t work fine together, Hero have too many text that is in Origin, Heroic Knacks, description of the denizens, some qualities. I do like the idea of one book to rule than all, but Hero doesn\u2019t, neither does Origin, so they could focus on what\u2019s new and not copy paste of so many texts. Copying text could cause contraditiction as one is corrected and the other no (as it happened to Kitsune and some of the permanent conditions of the denizens).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s annoying go thru 3 books as we needed to do to build a god (or even a Hero with some exotic knacks) on 1e, but it\u2019s the best way to keep the books working fine together.<br /> <br /> Now the good part, I liked a lot the new arts, the 2 old Shen and the young one playing risk made me laugh more than I would like to admit, not a big deal, but... The new \u201cstandardised\u201d experience cost make the use of Edges and skill tricks possible, as it really annoyed me they are not available, Origin and Heroes need the more human side to be ready...<br /> <br /> The way they described the scales is much much much more clear than before, and Tiers are described apart of it, making it clear that they are not the same thing. I didn\u2019t read thru everything, actually Inwent straight to the points that were not clear before, so many thing that were clear in my mind (it doesn\u2019t mean it was working before, just that I had a proper image of it)...<br /> In the next few days I intend to go thru Origin properly, and latter Hero... until there I will go easy on the critics...</div> </div> </div> </div>See, here's the thing. If you assume this is the final product, then there's still a lot of work to do and it falls short in a few areas.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER!<br /> <br /> You know what this DOES read like? A <b>work-in-progress</b>.<br /> <br /> Like it's a middle step between the Post-Layout samples the Backers got and the final product, when the Errata was collected and was in the process of being implemented. There's some clearer rules on Creature Life levels, some clearer examples on Scale, better things on what exactly is a Feat of Scale is, and the Hero Chargen actually is built from the sense of making a Hero from scratch rather than converting an Origin character.<br /> <br /> But there are still things that needed updating, which yeah... Feels like THIS was a draft where part of the errata was put in and more of it was to come. That's why I say &quot;Maybe this isn't the FINAL final version-&quot; and why I'm willing to wait on Neall to make an official comment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T00:21:37-07:00","id":1302490,"title":"","content":"I'm so much happy I buy only PDFs for first print of the books, until they are testes for few months later...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T03:14:30-07:00","id":1302507,"title":"","content":"Agree it\u2019s a work in progress, there are lots of mistakes in the final that are prety easy to fix, I do believe they were all listed on the errata tread.<br /> We were expecting a great impeccable book, as we payed for it about 2 years ago(?) and remained in silent for sooo long until the first draft and we were able to help (not by giving money) but by finding errors and bad explanations (I honestly joined the formum just for the errata, but I could not help as they left me waiting the subscription for 2 weeks), all the gross mistakes were found and should be fixed, and suddenly, they were not... that\u2019s frustating...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T06:41:14-07:00","id":1302538,"title":"","content":"The current silence might mean anything. It's possible that they indeed sent the wrong one, or maybe they sent the right one, but the printer used the wrong one. The radio silence could mean deliberation or it could mean that Neall is just being Neall and he's doing all the things at the same time. So I think it would be wise to stop panicking and getting angry over something that might not be happening.<br /> <br /> Now, knowing this. If it was Onyx Path's mistake, we might be stuck with the defective product, I don't think reprinting all the books would be cheap. If it's the printer's fault, maybe they're trying to get a reprint. Heck, depending on Onyx Path's finances, we might even get a corrected product even if it would have been Onyx Path's fault.<br /> <br /> Basically, it's too soon to be panicking when we don't have all the relevant details.<br /> <br /> All we can surmise is that they are looking into it, and will probably give us news soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","user":"Monkeydjie","date":". 04-04-2019, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T07:03:28-07:00","id":1302542,"title":"","content":"Except that it says (final version) on the PDF file from Drivethrurpg, or did as of last night when I checked. That doesn't indicate &quot;work in progress&quot; to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T07:23:54-07:00","id":1302545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1302542#post1302542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that it says (final version) on the PDF file from Drivethrurpg, or did as of last night when I checked. That doesn't indicate &quot;work in progress&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The deluxe version printers are a different company than DTRPG. It is entirely possible a different file got sent to each. Again, patience is the best approach here. For all we know, OPP is having the shipper open up boxes, taking pictures of pages in the book, and sending them to OPP to find out if the wrong file got printed. The relaunch of Scion is a BIG DEAL for OPP. They're going to make sure then know the full story before they start making decisions and communicating. Give them time to do the proper research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T04:57:06-07:00","id":1303050,"title":"","content":"Why don't these pdfs have the backers in them, the dragon blooded pdf, for comparison sake, does have it, and they couldn't have possibly missed that could they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T09:20:05-07:00","id":1303091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303050#post1303050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't these pdfs have the backers in them, the dragon blooded pdf, for comparison sake, does have it, and they couldn't have possibly missed that could they?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s supposed to...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T10:49:46-07:00","id":1303118,"title":"","content":"Indeed... that\u2019s a reason to believe it\u2019s not the final one. It\u2019s part of the KS Pledges description that the name would be there.<br /> <br /> By itself that lacking of the names is a failure in the delivery of the project...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T11:55:12-07:00","id":1303146,"title":"","content":"We were told that the wait was to make the book perfect. It isn't. They ignored a majority of errors for word count well... if the books need more pages to make it perfect do it. We paid for the book to be immaculate not sub par and a lil communication would be great thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T13:38:57-07:00","id":1303167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303146#post1303146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were told that the wait was to make the book perfect. It isn't. They ignored a majority of errors for word count well... if the books need more pages to make it perfect do it. We paid for the book to be immaculate not sub par and a lil communication would be great thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Before this goes on much further, no book is error-free. That is not something we ever promised, because 33 years of making RPG books informs us that it can not be done. You did not pay for anything immaculate, you pledged to help us create the best books we could. Right now, we\u2019re trying to figure out what happened to erase a bunch of the work a whole lot of people did, including our backers, to fix those errors we could fix, but while we\u2019re doing that, please don\u2019t go changing the goalposts on us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T13:43:25-07:00","id":1303169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303167#post1303167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before this goes on much further, no book is error-free. That is not something we ever promised, because 33 years of making RPG books informs us that it can not be done. You did not pay for anything immaculate, you pledged to help us create the best books we could. Right now, we\u2019re trying to figure out what happened to erase a bunch of the work a whole lot of people did, including our backers, to fix those errors we could fix, but while we\u2019re doing that, please don\u2019t go changing the goalposts on us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for letting us know the issue is being addressed Rich, it makes me for one feel a lot better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T16:01:46-07:00","id":1303208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303167#post1303167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before this goes on much further, no book is error-free. That is not something we ever promised, because 33 years of making RPG books informs us that it can not be done. You did not pay for anything immaculate, you pledged to help us create the best books we could. Right now, we\u2019re trying to figure out what happened to erase a bunch of the work a whole lot of people did, including our backers, to fix those errors we could fix, but while we\u2019re doing that, please don\u2019t go changing the goalposts on us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your answer, Rich. I am not looking for perfection, there is no such thing, and I believe the reasonable people are not looking for it too. There is always corrections and the way Onyx Path does (allowing us to help on the errata) is amazing, I do enjoy being part of it (even not being part of those erratas specifically).<br /> <br /> I thank again to notice we are lost here. If you say you (as a team) did corrections and they are not in our books, I think there was a problem and you can solve it. I hope all that were printed is not lost. I hope too, that all the work done was not lost by a computer mistake os something like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T11:10:25-07:00","id":1303365,"title":"","content":"Hey Rich. Thanks for touching in and letting us know you guys are aware of it.<br /> <br /> Any and all updates on the situation you can provide would be wonderful. My table has been sitting on the Scion 2E for months now and we were just starting to prepare our game when we found out the books printing had been finished. Most of the table didn't want to learn the system and such before the final touches were on it because they thought it might be confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T22:36:02-07:00","id":1303717,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">edit: Okay my formatting is being dumb hold on-</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">We got a statement in the Monday Meeting Notes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rich T.</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today, though, we were less happy with having to get together during the meeting and talk about how we need to figure out what broke in our proofing process with our Scion 2e core books.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll talk more about this when we get all the information in, but it seems pretty sure that a number of errata fixes that Neall input did not \u201cstick\u201d, but remained as errors. He is currently, painstakingly, going back through his errata notes and reconstructing what changes need to be made.<br /> <br /> The last I checked, he hasn\u2019t found a pattern for why some changes stayed, and others did not, nor why this happened with these two books, but not on the dozen-plus books that have previously used the same proofing process. While I\u2019d like to know that, and will, our in-house devs have already taken over the errata input phase so that our book developers only have to notate the PDF.<br /> <br /> This will add another stage, but will also give us an additional chance to identify whether errata that we gathered is actually in a book.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll be able to tell better once Neall finishes his pass, but we\u2019re not seeing anything that breaks the game or makes it unplayable. Certainly, the rules as they stand have worked for the many Scion 2e groups who are already playing the game, including the fraction of Actual Play groups we can highlight each week in our Media section below.<br /> <br /> But it is extremely frustrating for us, and Neall, but also for all of the Scion community that stepped up to pore through the Backer PDF and send us what they found. Sometimes, in publishing, despite all your safeguards, stuff slips in. Here\u2019s a painful example of a process that worked\u2026until it didn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-09-2019, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T00:44:11-07:00","id":1303730,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m glad it\u2019s an acknowledged issue, and thanks to Neall\u2019s hardwork we will definitely be getting the fixed PDFs! Still unknown based on Rich\u2019s statement whether whatever happened to the file happened before or after it went to press though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T05:38:29-07:00","id":1303757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The last I checked, he hasn\u2019t found a pattern for why some changes stayed, and others did not, nor why this happened with these two books, but not on the dozen-plus books that have previously used the same proofing process.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> So... Use of a Chaos Marvel confirmed?<br /> <br /> Glad they are trying to fix all these problems. I understand both sides of this. Yes, the writers, editors, designers are human. This kind of thing CAN happen. And it did. I understand too that is frustrating for us to wait all this time and receive a &quot;final pdf&quot; still not corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T05:50:49-07:00","id":1303759,"title":"","content":"The pdf isn\u2019t the issue, those can always be upgraded, the issue is the question about the print version. We all would like to have our physical books with the errata applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T05:58:11-07:00","id":1303760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303730#post1303730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m glad it\u2019s an acknowledged issue, and thanks to Neall\u2019s hardwork we will definitely be getting the fixed PDFs! Still unknown based on Rich\u2019s statement whether whatever happened to the file happened before or after it went to press though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the comments, Rich made is sound like they don't know if the printed books have been affected. They're trying to figure out what errata was applied and what wasn't in order to know what to check in the printed books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T08:20:40-07:00","id":1303782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303759#post1303759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pdf isn\u2019t the issue, those can always be upgraded, the issue is the question about the print version. We all would like to have our physical books with the errata applied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes we would. However I wouldn\u2019t dismiss the labor cost of them going back and fixing the file currently. There was no guarantee that was going to happen, and a lot of companies in the historynof the industry would have doubled down and insisted that was the intended finished product, especially if it matches the printed book. So i\u2019m relieved to effectively have it guaranteed now that we\u2019re getting the fixed content one way or another, and grateful to Neall for putting in the work to address the problem!<br /> <br /> That said, I would strongly recommend to OPP that they take the lesson here and don\u2019t send the file to the printers until AFTER if it\u2019s gone to the Backers in the future!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T10:21:54-07:00","id":1303798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303782#post1303782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I would strongly recommend to OPP that they take the lesson here and don\u2019t send the file to the printers until AFTER if it\u2019s gone to the Backers in the future!</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s an extra layer of proofing... it doesn\u2019t solve printing issues, as there are always things that happen weird on the printing... but it solves most of the formatting and text issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T10:27:10-07:00","id":1303800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303798#post1303798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s an extra layer of proofing... it doesn\u2019t solve printing issues, as there are always things that happen weird on the printing... but it solves most of the formatting and text issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but this issue here was some sort of corruption of their file as opposed to something that happened at the printer. Hence me referring to the lesson in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T14:50:14-07:00","id":1303831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303798#post1303798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s an extra layer of proofing... it doesn\u2019t solve printing issues, as there are always things that happen weird on the printing... but it solves most of the formatting and text issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I worked in the printing industry for many years in pre-production. Mistakes like this rarely happen during the printing process. When printers send a proof out to a customer or create off-set plates those are created using rasterd post script files (RIPs). These files are pixelated images, they have no knowledge of fonts or previous versions of the original file. If changes are dictated, the RIP is discarded and the changes are made to the originating file and then a brand new RIP is made.<br /> <br /> If the hardcopies are indeed made from a pre-errata file then more than likely that the mistake occured in pre-production (whether by the printer or by OPP) and that someone at OPP approved a proof for production that was incorrect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T17:58:38-07:00","id":1303853,"title":"","content":"Jeremysbrain, That\u2019s the kind of problem I am mentioning. I work with cultural events, so we are always printing folders, fliers and things like that. There are moments you get a wrong Pantone, the cut lines don\u2019t match, things like this.<br /> <br /> Glamourweaver, I agree with you, the problem here is the kind that can be solving by a \u201cpre-print\u201d review by the backers, give a week before printing and you probably get a ton of misses in less than one day (as we had in this case).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T18:05:54-07:00","id":1303854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303782#post1303782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes we would. However I wouldn\u2019t dismiss the labor cost of them going back and fixing the file currently. There was no guarantee that was going to happen, and a lot of companies in the historynof the industry would have doubled down and insisted that was the intended finished product, especially if it matches the printed book. So i\u2019m relieved to effectively have it guaranteed now that we\u2019re getting the fixed content one way or another, and grateful to Neall for putting in the work to address the problem!<br /> <br /> That said, I would strongly recommend to OPP that they take the lesson here and don\u2019t send the file to the printers until AFTER if it\u2019s gone to the Backers in the future!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m happy that the PDF will be fixed, and grateful Neall is taking care of us.<br /> <br /> On the subject of your recommendation, I agree. I\u2019m kind of frustrated because people asked for the final PDF version after the Kickstarter hardcopies went into production. They were told they had to wait until the POD proofs were approved, in case there were more mistakes. Which is confusing, because what mistakes were anticipated? Layout mistakes or game content mistakes? Because the KS books were already in production. We could have raised a red flag weeks earlier.<br /> <br /> I posted to the Monday Meeting blog. No name calling. No accusations. It didn\u2019t make it past moderation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T22:31:04-07:00","id":1303894,"title":"","content":"As a Backerkit backer for the physical books, I'm hoping OPP will at least send me vouchers to get the books in PoD &quot;at cost&quot; when those files are corrected. Because I certainly won't buy them again at full whack in a later print run after this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","name":"Jargogle Bamboozle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T03:46:28-07:00","id":1303909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303854#post1303854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I posted to the Monday Meeting blog. No name calling. No accusations. It didn\u2019t make it past moderation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sure everyone at Onyx Path is extremely aware of what did and did not happen to get us here and saw no point in such a post that would only serve to highlight any delays in an actual answer to what is the next step.<br /> <br /> This is probably hitting them in the gut right now. Scion 2E is their first traditional print run for their own property using their own system and given the number of kickstarters they've run, this happens to their own property... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T04:37:25-07:00","id":1303912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303909#post1303909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am sure everyone at Onyx Path is extremely aware of what did and did not happen to get us here and saw no point in such a post that would only serve to highlight any delays in an actual answer to what is the next step.<br /> <br /> This is probably hitting them in the gut right now. Scion 2E is their first traditional print run for their own property using their own system and given the number of kickstarters they've run, this happens to their own property... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose. I\u2019m not unreasonable and I\u2019m not crying censorship. The fact that someone didn\u2019t approve my comment doesn\u2019t outrage me, life goes on. I will say I\u2019m not thrilled with Rich\u2019s tone in the comments section coupled with the suppression, but... eh. I do get the rationale of not letting things get out of hand until he has more definitive information.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I\u2019ll write more later, but it\u2019s 5:30 am here. I\u2019m going back to bed. Seems prudent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T04:44:34-07:00","id":1303913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303909#post1303909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am sure everyone at Onyx Path is extremely aware of what did and did not happen to get us here and saw no point in such a post that would only serve to highlight any delays in an actual answer to what is the next step.<br /> <br /> This is probably hitting them in the gut right now. Scion 2E is their first traditional print run for their own property using their own system and given the number of kickstarters they've run, this happens to their own property... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is not much we can do now, if we want the book to be fixed, we need to wait. As you said, Scion is not another one of the projects, it\u2019s the first book using their system, it\u2019s another entire line to be explored (a line that is recognised by the market by it self, no need for the marketing effort at same level as Pugmire and Maus), it\u2019s a real big deal for them, and they are not going to screw up.<br /> <br /> Neal and the team are professionals, we know their work and we know they will do their best...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T16:45:56-07:00","id":1304043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303909#post1303909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am sure everyone at Onyx Path is extremely aware of what did and did not happen to get us here and......<br /> <br /> This is probably hitting them in the gut right now. Scion 2E is their first traditional print run for their own property using their own system and given the number of kickstarters they've run, this happens to their own property... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I would caution against taking the tone of, \u201cNobody is more upset about this then Onyx Path.\u201d That sentiment may have it\u2019s place, but it\u2019s not appropriate in this situation. I do agree that they\u2019re probably horrified and frustrated. I do have sympathy for them, but it\u2019s time for some accountability. Part of that involves listening.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ll note I excised part of your quote pertaining to blog moderation. I\u2019m not cherry picking your words, I am conceding the point to you. I can see wanting to do some damage control till Rich has some more information, but I\u2019m going to post here in a polite and responsible manner. My intention is to keep my concerns within the Onyx Path family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1303913#post1303913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neal and the team are professionals, we know their work and we know they will do their best...</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you wholeheartedly and without qualification. That said, a critique of this situation is not by default an indictment of Neall Price. I see this situation as being well above his pay grade as a freelance content developer. No one need defend him to me.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t entirely a response to you, Mateus, I\u2019m seeing it a lot. We can\u2019t equate everything that isn\u2019t glowingly positive in this situation as a personal attack upon Neall. It gets in the way of having a mature conversation.<br /> <br /> Defending someone who isn\u2019t accused, is a distraction, whether its unintended or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T17:38:40-07:00","id":1304052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1304043#post1304043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn\u2019t entirely a response to you, Mateus, I\u2019m seeing it a lot. We can\u2019t equate everything that isn\u2019t glowingly positive in this situation as a personal attack upon Neall. It gets in the way of having a mature conversation.<br /> <br /> Defending someone who isn\u2019t accused, is a distraction, whether its unintended or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading my post after reading yours made me understand what you mean, I was not actually defending Neal (I actually did it, but not intended to), my intentions were to calm the exaltation the people have in the last week... even myself...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T17:55:57-07:00","id":1304053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1304052#post1304052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading my post after reading yours made me understand what you mean, I was not actually defending Neal (I actually did it, but not intended to), my intentions were to calm the exaltation the people have in the last week... even myself...</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s fine, friend. Defending Neall is actually fine. I\u2019m just asking other folks to not assume that Neall is being blamed, unless he specifically is called out.<br /> <br /> And reassurance is great too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T07:37:21-07:00","id":1306249,"title":"","content":"Agreed. The situation is very unfortunate and Rich, Neall and the team aren't happy about it but they are trying to fix what they can. And they are making adjustments to prevent something like this in the future. That's really all we can ask of them in a situation like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T17:27:03-07:00","id":1306366,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd say that they need to make &quot;PoD At Cost&quot; available to all physical book backers now. <br /> <br /> Plenty of folks asked for the final PDFs to be released *before* the books were printed, but OPP decided not to. Ironically, all of this could've been caught if they actually had. <br /> <br /> Now, their new process sounds like the one they used for Pugmire and Mau, and that worked well, so I'm glad they're adopting it for their other lines. The forum approach was always awkward and clunky. Also, not having the devs check final print proofs thoroughly (as appears to be the case) was a bit of an oversight, so glad they're going forward with that too. <br /> <br /> However, physical book backers (which was the whole thrust of this KS) including those on Backerkit (like myself) should not have to fork out the full whack again for a corrected print in light of all of this. OPP can offer corrected PoD prints at cost to backers via DTRPG, and I'd say that would be a good approach. The book backers then have a chance to get the corrected books cheaper, it doesn't cost OPP extra money (they just forego the profit from those PODs), and it's a decent good will gesture too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","user":"Jargogle Bamboozle","date":". 04-20-2019, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","name":"Jargogle Bamboozle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T22:43:56-07:00","id":1306437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jargogle Bamboozle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1306366#post1306366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd say that they need to make &quot;PoD At Cost&quot; available to all physical book backers now.<br /> <br /> Plenty of folks asked for the final PDFs to be released *before* the books were printed, but OPP decided not to. Ironically, all of this could've been caught if they actually had.<br /> <br /> Now, their new process sounds like the one they used for Pugmire and Mau, and that worked well, so I'm glad they're adopting it for their other lines. The forum approach was always awkward and clunky. Also, not having the devs check final print proofs thoroughly (as appears to be the case) was a bit of an oversight, so glad they're going forward with that too.<br /> <br /> However, physical book backers (which was the whole thrust of this KS) including those on Backerkit (like myself) should not have to fork out the full whack again for a corrected print in light of all of this. OPP can offer corrected PoD prints at cost to backers via DTRPG, and I'd say that would be a good approach. The book backers then have a chance to get the corrected books cheaper, it doesn't cost OPP extra money (they just forego the profit from those PODs), and it's a decent good will gesture too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, anyone getting a physical book gets at-cost coupons, dude. That's always part of the physical tiers.<br /> <br /> Dunno about Backerkit pre-orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T23:42:30-07:00","id":1306449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1306437#post1306437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, anyone getting a physical book gets at-cost coupons, dude. That's always part of the physical tiers.<br /> <br /> Dunno about Backerkit pre-orders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Backerkit pre-orders for the physical books don't, sadly, and we don't get PDFs either unless we pay extra for them. I have forked out $153 (USD) to order the two books (pdfs not included) via Backerkit and get them delivered to New Zealand. If people who were involved in the Kickstarter directly for physical books feel irked, imagine how those of us (and there are many) who backed via Backerkit feel... No PoDs at cost, no pdfs, no extras, more expensive, just the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","user":"Jargogle Bamboozle","date":". 04-21-2019, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","name":"Jargogle Bamboozle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T01:39:09-07:00","id":1306474,"title":"","content":"Can we... wait to see how bad the damage actually is? Rich's last comments imply that the amount of errata that didn't make it into the book is bad, but not catastrophic either. If it's a few pages of a GoogleDoc or whatever, worrying about getting a whole new book is a bit extreme.<br /> <br /> If I can print out all the corrections that didn't get in on a single double sided page of paper, I'm not ordering another copy just to have those put in. It sucks, but even if it was an at-cost PoD and shipping was covered it still wouldn't be worth the money to me. And I'd imagine more people feel the same than not on that.<br /> <br /> I don't have some specific page count in mind, but if an errata file sent to all of us is too big to be used practically at the table... then it seems worth pressing about things like at-cost PoD copies for people that didn't get those in the KS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T00:05:19-07:00","id":1307161,"title":"","content":"I would love to be wrong, but I'm bracing myself for extensive errata. Were it within typical norms it likely wouldn't have taken so long, they wouldn't have said it's not as bad as the latest edition of Shadowrun (roundly regarded as one of the most appallingly edited RPGs out there, so that's a really low bar to set), and they probably wouldn't need extra time to prepare a statement about it. Of course, the real tough one to deal with will be if the Backer List is missing from the print, because that was one of the principle awards for being a backer.<br /> <br /> My personal tolerance is a single double-sided sheet with a reasonable font size (i.e. not crammed with 8pt. text and no spacing). Beyond that starts to get unwieldy at the table and slows things down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","user":"Jargogle Bamboozle","date":". 04-23-2019, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","name":"Jargogle Bamboozle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T01:31:59-07:00","id":1307176,"title":"","content":"Bracing yourself and setting your expectations where you feel is best based on the information on hand is fine.<br /> <br /> I'm calling for not doing things like demanding everyone get free at-cost PoD coupons now before we know more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T07:05:57-07:00","id":1307210,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm just glad they are acknowledging the problem and sending out an errata sheet straight away. Expecting them to go into financial distress by offering freebies because of what was, in the end, an error in a process that has always worked before, isn't reasonable. They had a problem, fixed what they could, took the path of honesty, kept us in the loop, and learned from it. I don't think we can (or should) expect more. I will just be happy to have the books in my hand - I can deal with typos pretty easily. After experiences with other games and kickstarters, I'm not going to rage over an unavoidable mistake/process breakdown when it's all been handled so professionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T10:41:03-07:00","id":1307248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307176#post1307176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bracing yourself and setting your expectations where you feel is best based on the information on hand is fine.<br /> <br /> I'm calling for not doing things like demanding everyone get free at-cost PoD coupons now before we know more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who backed the Kickstarter is getting PoD coupons anyway. Only backerkit preorders are in question on that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T11:59:58-07:00","id":1307268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307210#post1307210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm just glad they are acknowledging the problem and sending out an errata sheet straight away. Expecting them to go into financial distress by offering freebies because of what was, in the end, an error in a process that has always worked before, isn't reasonable. They had a problem, fixed what they could, took the path of honesty, kept us in the loop, and learned from it. I don't think we can (or should) expect more. I will just be happy to have the books in my hand - I can deal with typos pretty easily. After experiences with other games and kickstarters, I'm not going to rage over an unavoidable mistake/process breakdown when it's all been handled so professionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you\u2019re on the internet? Because this stance seems far too reasonable and measured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12472-foozle","name":"Foozle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T12:14:50-07:00","id":1307274,"title":"","content":"Hah! \ud83d\ude0a Yep, I'm on the internet. I've also worked in retail for far too many years to blame people for unavoidable glitches in production (unless they deny, avoid, and blame-place themselves, of course...). I'm just looking forward to my books. Whether God X has the right purview or not is something I can just change myself if it becomes important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:59:48-07:00","id":1307391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307210#post1307210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm just glad they are acknowledging the problem and sending out an errata sheet straight away. Expecting them to go into financial distress by offering freebies because of what was, in the end, an error in a process that has always worked before, isn't reasonable. They had a problem, fixed what they could, took the path of honesty, kept us in the loop, and learned from it. I don't think we can (or should) expect more. I will just be happy to have the books in my hand - I can deal with typos pretty easily. After experiences with other games and kickstarters, I'm not going to rage over an unavoidable mistake/process breakdown when it's all been handled so professionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>What financial distress do they incur by offering Backerkit backers the PoDs at cost if the errata is extensive? At cost means that we pay for the production and shipping. It doesn't cost OPP anything, unless you are saying that Backerkit backers (who don't even get the PDFs, remember, or any of the KS extras) should put even more money into it just to get an extra option the KS backers already have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","name":"Jargogle Bamboozle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T21:00:59-07:00","id":1307402,"title":"","content":"IIRC (Someone that knows OBS's fees feel free to correct me) there's still a small fee charged.<br /> <br /> Though KS backers have every right to feel entitled to get things people that didn't back get, or get it cheaper... they're the ones that put their money up for risk, and those things are their rewards for doing so. Jumping on the Backerkit to preorder the product is just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T21:42:53-07:00","id":1307410,"title":"","content":"It cost them money to investigate and fix what they could, over and above planned expenses. It will cost more money to assemble an errata sheet. I doubt that the errors are &quot;extensive&quot; (though everyone probably has their own definition of that word), so I strongly suspect an errata sheet will solve the problem in the best compromise possible. If they start distributing &quot;at-cost&quot; replacements of Scion, that costs them more capitol, and no gaming company has really deep pockets. But honestly, until we actually get the final update from Neall later this week, all speculation (good and bad) is just that - speculation. I suggest we all wait and see what they are going to do before we start trying to tell them what we think they <i>should </i>do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T23:10:22-07:00","id":1307419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307410#post1307410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If they start distributing &amp;quot;at-cost&amp;quot; replacements of Scion, that costs them more capitol, and no gaming company has really deep pockets. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>But we ARE getting at-cost coupons. If you backed the Kickstarter and got a physical book, you get coupons. It\u2019s standard.<br /> <br /> I quote:<br /> <br /> \u201cAn option to purchase both the Scion: Origin and Scion: Hero Print on Demand (PoD) physical books as close to cost as we can give you (see description in the text to the left)\u201d<br /> <br /> All physical tiers get that.<br /> <br /> If a coupon is what is wanted, only Backerkit preorders need to worry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T06:03:30-07:00","id":1307448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307402#post1307402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though KS backers have every right to feel entitled to get things people that didn't back get, or get it cheaper... they're the ones that put their money up for risk, and those things are their rewards for doing so. Jumping on the Backerkit to preorder the product is just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a bit sanctimonious from a big picture perspective. There are lots of reasons why someone might use Backerkit. Maybe cash flow was a problem, perhaps they didn\u2019t hear about the Kickstarter, or they just had a change of heart. Sure, Kickstarter backers are important, but we can honor them without judging people who use Backerkit. I write that as a Scion KS backer. Frankly, ttrpgs rely on communities. Every game sold is possibly an introduction to someone who has never bought a Scion book before and might feel called to do so. I\u2019d like to see Scion grow in popularity so that it receives more publishing support and additional products, and getting the game out there and actually played is vital. Do I think all Backerkit folks should get backer benefits like POD at-cost printing? No. But this is not a normal situation either. If Bamboozle wants to politely vent some frustration or ask about POD consideration, let him. The worst that can happen is OP says no.<br /> <br /> I tell ya, I ABSOLUTELY expect the crowdsourced errata phase to be part of the normal development cycle for these books. The following quote from Rich Thomas really annoyed the heck out of me (from an April 16th comment on the April 15th Monday Meeting Blog). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rich Thomas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But whatever we do, if we\u2019re looking at those reverted fixes and think they are not what we wanted but are non-critical, and some backers are thinking that the errata phase was vital to making the books the books we wanted to create, then we have a disconnect we don\u2019t want to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no disconnect. Errata sheets suck ass. Avoiding as much errata as possible has nothing to do with trying to obtain perfection. I do thank community volunteers who perform additional proofing. I DO expect their legitimate findings to be implemented in the final document. This IS specifically part of the overall process that I\u2019m backing when I make a KS pledge. If the crowdsourced errata collection phase were to stop, my inclination to buy a first run hard cover would be severely hampered.<br /> <br /> Now before anybody proscribes a course of action for me, I\u2019ve made my own peace with the situation. Mistakes do happen. Onyx Path\u2019s dismay and frustration comes across as quite sincere. It irritates me however, to watch some of you folks dogpile on someone for being unhappy about it while that person tries to come to a conclusion they can live with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T09:27:30-07:00","id":1307499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307448#post1307448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s a bit sanctimonious from a big picture perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd quibble about the adjective choice, but ultimately it's true and important for the big picture. Backers get more than per-orders or regular purchase later. That's part of enticement to get people to back a project. If we're going to talk about someone trying to figure out a &quot;conclusion they can live with,&quot; remembering the specific hierarchy of rewards that's inherent to the problem should be part of that thought process. It's not even something you disagree with.<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but we can honor them without judging people who use Backerkit. </div> </div> </div>What judgement did I lay on people who pre-ordered through Backerkit?<br /> <br /> I was saying &quot;yes&quot; to this question. &quot;It doesn't cost OPP anything, unless you are saying that Backerkit backers (...) should put even more money into it just to get an extra option the KS backers already have? &quot;<br /> <br /> It's the answer you'd give too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Bamboozle wants to politely vent some frustration or ask about POD consideration, let him. </div> </div> </div>As I already addressed, my issue was him demanding PoD-at-cost now. That's not venting frustration. That's not politely asking about the option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no disconnect. </div> </div> </div>I don't know... your whole response seems to be a disconnect here. Rich and you both clearly think the crowdsourcing of proofing is a good thing (Rich keeps doing it for his company's products after all, even if it messes up, which leads him to work on refining the process to avoid those mistakes in the future). When he says that it isn't vital to making the books... it's not. People have been making RPG books for decades without it. You're responding as if this means Rich wants to stop it despite any work or headaches (and lets face it he and his team have gotten some rather nasty comments about changes that didn't make the final cut), even as he's still talking about making the process better. How is a disconnect not apparently the case here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It irritates me however, to watch some of you folks dogpile on someone for being unhappy about it while that person tries to come to a conclusion they can live with. </div> </div> </div>It frustrates me that you read the posts so shallowly that you think this is at all a fair assessment of what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-24-2019, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:04:15-07:00","id":1307619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307499#post1307499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd quibble about the adjective choice, but ultimately it's true and important for the big picture. Backers get more than per-orders or regular purchase later. That's part of enticement to get people to back a project. If we're going to talk about someone trying to figure out a &amp;quot;conclusion they can live with,&amp;quot; remembering the specific hierarchy of rewards that's inherent to the problem should be part of that thought process. It's not even something you disagree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before I reply to the body of your post, I\u2019d like to draw your attention to something. This use of phrases like <i>\u201cit\u2019s not even something you disagree with\u201d</i>, of.. <i>\u201cit\u2019s the answer you\u2019d give too.\u201d</i> President Trump has that habit when he\u2019s trying to refute a question from the Press. He makes a biased declarative statement to a reporter and tacks on \u201cand you know it!\u201d Or \u201cyou know it\u2019s true!\u201d Like he\u2019s trying to do a Jedi mind trick. Anyway, why don\u2019t you let me tell you (and anybody else reading) what I think and what I do or don\u2019t disagree with?<br /> <br /> To the quoted paragraph above, you\u2019re half-right, except you didn\u2019t quote or respond to an important part of what I wrote. You\u2019re correct, I don\u2019t think pre-orders should get the benefits of Kickstarter backers. I also said <u>this was not a normal situation.</u> You skated right past that with nary a word and it\u2019s integral to the point I was making. This is not business as usual. I didn\u2019t think I needed to spell it out, but that means I don\u2019t think all the normal rules should apply in this specific case. That guy bought those books in good faith that they\u2019d go through the crowdsourced errata phases in order to be the best books possible. Whether you and Rich choose to accept it, many people feel that is an important step. I know that I have much greater confidence in an Onyx Path book knowing that it\u2019s going to go through that process. I know what happened with Scion was a mistake and an accident, but he\u2019s not asking for a refund, he just wants some help. Furthermore, he\u2019s not asking me and he\u2019s not asking you. If Onyx Path doesn\u2019t want to do it, so be it. <br /> <br /> You ever see <i>Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade</i>? The scene where the sheriff arrives and young Indy has to give the artifact back to the tomb raiders? And one of them gives Indy what would become his iconic hat and says, <b>\u201cYou don\u2019t win \u2018em all kid, but you don\u2019t have to like it.\u201d</b> That\u2019s a generous part of what I\u2019m trying to communicate here. He doesn\u2019t have to like it and he doesn\u2019t need you to tell him how S-O-L he is. I think he knows. You\u2019ve spelled that out really well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What judgement did I lay on people who pre-ordered through Backerkit?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re actually fine all the way to Post #51. At post #53 and #59, you take an unpleasant turn. First, in post #53 you start to characterize Bamboozle as \u201cdemanding\u201d things. That\u2019s emotionally loading language designed to characterize the speaker. I could write that he\u2019s \u201cdesperately pleading for help\u201d and it would be every bit as hyperbolic. He\u2019s ASKING for some consideration that he admits he knows he\u2019s not entitled to, plus he\u2019s frustrated. He spent a lot of money for something that is not what he reasonably expected to receive and he\u2019s got no recourse. Is he pointed? Yeah. Does he come from a perspective of feeling wronged? Yeah. Demanding??? I think you\u2019re being a little sensitive on Onyx Path\u2019s behalf. What you see as demanding, I see as worried and disappointed. <br /> <br /> If you want a quote.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though KS backers have every right to feel entitled to get things people that didn't back get, or get it cheaper... they're the ones that put their money up for risk, and those things are their rewards for doing so. Jumping on the Backerkit to preorder the product is just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is judgmental. First, not all Kickstarters are alike. An Onyx Path Kickstarter, despite some past problems including this errata situation, is not much of a risk. They\u2019ve always delivered and created a lot of great content. More importantly, you don\u2019t know why anybody uses Backerkit. You don\u2019t know why they didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter. The guy spent $153 bucks for two books to New Zealand only to find out he may have to annotate his new books or fill them with post-it notes, and he gets nothing else. No PDF. Then you drop whatever you\u2019re doing and write (in some many words) that it\u2019s his fault for being a Backerkit Pre-order. That may be true, but why do you need to be the guy who tells him? Why are you surprised that someone called you out?<br /> <br /> You want more examples of being judgmental?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I already addressed, my issue was him demanding PoD-at-cost now. That's not venting frustration. That's not politely asking about the option.</div> </div> </div> </div>He\u2019s not any more demanding than innumerable other people when they ask for stuff. If I take a defective product back to a store, I\u2019m technically demanding compensation but I do actually make it a request instead. Like many people in his situation, he\u2019s afraid the answer will be no, so he makes his case rather earnestly and pulls on strings of feeling cheated and the hope that someone will cut him a break, if only out of good will. Plus you\u2019re hung up with him \u2018demanding\u2019 this <i>\u201cright now\u201d</i>. Dude, you\u2019re projecting that on to him. I re-read his post to make sure. Yeah, he does use the word \u2018now\u2019, but it\u2019s in the context of \u201cNow that we know that there will not be a correction to the books, I\u2019d hope that Pre-Orders could get some help with the at-cost POD option that backers can get.\u201d It\u2019s a signifier that the situation has now evolved, because we\u2019d gotten more information at that point. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was saying &amp;quot;yes&amp;quot; to this question. &amp;quot;It doesn't cost OPP anything, unless you are saying that Backerkit backers (...) should put even more money into it just to get an extra option the KS backers already have? &amp;quot;<br /> <br /> It's the answer you'd give too.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you\u2019re completely wrong. First of all, it\u2019s not my company and not my decision. But that\u2019s a weasel answer and I don\u2019t like those, even though I think that\u2019s fair to point out. If it was my company I would talk to my financial folks and look at the impact of offering POD at-cost for Backerkit folks who got a prestige hard copy. If it hurt the company, I\u2019d explain that I couldn\u2019t help. If it didn\u2019t make that big of an impact, I\u2019d let them get POD at-cost as a goodwill gesture. I\u2019d also reinforce that this was a special situation and not likely to happen again. That the integrity of Kickstarter rewards needs to be upheld as not to disincentivize the Kickstarter. Then I\u2019d add a few sentences to the already long Kickstarter disclaimer that says the crowdsourced errata sweep will continue to be done in good faith, but ultimately the product will be delivered \u201cas is\u201d after the standard thorough in-house development and editing. This PLUS all the new procedures Rich already mentioned to hopefully eliminate the need for that disclaimer to be ever invoked. <br /> <br /> But telling a guy that it\u2019s his own fault for being a Backerkit pre-order instead of a KS backer? No, I wouldn\u2019t do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know... your whole response seems to be a disconnect here. Rich and you both clearly think the crowdsourcing of proofing is a good thing (Rich keeps doing it for his company's products after all, even if it messes up, which leads him to work on refining the process to avoid those mistakes in the future). When he says that it isn't vital to making the books... it's not. People have been making RPG books for decades without it. You're responding as if this means Rich wants to stop it despite any work or headaches (and lets face it he and his team have gotten some rather nasty comments about changes that didn't make the final cut), even as he's still talking about making the process better. How is a disconnect not apparently the case here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not responding to this as if Rich wants to stop it. You have misinterpreted what I meant, but I wrote in a conversational style, so maybe that\u2019s understandable. That paragraph is part of a reply to Rich that I\u2019ve been writing in my head for the last couple days. Where I quoted Rich was from a series of back and forth comments between Kyman and Rich. At one point Rich states that he never promised perfection because it\u2019s unobtainable. Kyman politely redirects that he didn\u2019t mean literal perfection, but a state where the books could be the best they reasonable could be (by virtue of having all the crowdsourced errata added), and he suggests that there has been a misunderstanding. Rich starts his reply with a two word sentence. \u201cNo misunderstanding.\u201d I didn\u2019t quote the whole paragraph, but that\u2019s where Rich makes his remark about there being a disconnect. Ergo, I wrote \u201cThere is no disconnect.\u201d That was my somewhat subconscious way of saying to Rich, \u201cThere is no misunderstanding.\u201d<br /> <br /> Exposition aside, I think he\u2019s got it wrong. I think you\u2019re wrong too. The crowdsourced errata phase is vital. Do I think one LITERALLY CANNOT MAKE an RPG without it? I hope you won\u2019t insult my intelligence. Of course you can. Yet, the overall quality of Onyx Path books has grown in leaps and bounds, and I have a lot more confidence in buying one of their RPGs based upon interesting content, without fear of broken rules or wondering if I should question whether something got missed in editing. It\u2019s been a good thing and he shouldn\u2019t minimize it because this Scion situation is unfortunate. Maybe he knows, but I\u2019d like him to hear my feedback anyway.<br /> <br /> And just because we made RPGs without this step for decades, doesn\u2019t mean I want to go backwards. I\u2019m not saying that to Rich, I\u2019m saying it to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It frustrates me that you read the posts so shallowly that you think this is at all a fair assessment of what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know if you\u2019re being snarky or sincere. If it\u2019s any consolation it frustrates me that two people thought your post deserved to be liked. On the bright side, I\u2019m a rando on the internet and you don\u2019t owe me anything. If you don\u2019t like what I wrote, soon it will be forgotten and life will go on. I\u2019ll soon forget too and probably not check the boards for a couple years. <br /> <br /> For what it\u2019s worth, I don\u2019t think you\u2019re a bad person. I think you\u2019re really invested in Onyx Path and you like their writers and developers and you don\u2019t want to see the company hurt. But circumstance has really screwed Bamboozle and it doesn\u2019t have to be his fault that it happened. Empathy doesn\u2019t have to be disloyalty. If I\u2019m wrong and you just like arguing with people, well... my time is just about up here anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T17:47:07-07:00","id":1307637,"title":"","content":"This is where I think it's worth pointing out that <i>none </i>of us can say we didn't get &quot;what we expected to receive&quot;, because none of us knows what we're going to get! The final books aren't here. The errata could be four lines, four pararaphs, or four pages. We don't know. Until we know, until we get Neall's official statement, until there is something to base our kudos or complaints on, all of this is just speculation and hand-wringing over a worst-case scenario that may never come to pass. Let's wait and see what happens - and maybe give Loki a little love to prevent this from happening again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T18:07:15-07:00","id":1307640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1307619#post1307619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">President Trump</div> </div> </div> </div>Sick burn bro.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, why don\u2019t you let me tell you (and anybody else reading) what I think and what I do or don\u2019t disagree with? </div> </div> </div>I did. You did in the post I responded to. You agreed with those things in your reply to me. &quot; Do I think all Backerkit folks should get backer benefits like POD at-cost printing? No.&quot; You already agreed with what I was saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That guy bought those books in good faith that they\u2019d go through the crowdsourced errata phases in order to be the best books possible. </div> </div> </div>And that's what happened, even though it got messed up at a stage after the crowdsourced errata pass. Are you trying to claim it didn't happen?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know what happened with Scion was a mistake and an accident, but he\u2019s not asking for a refund, he just wants some help. Furthermore, he\u2019s not asking me and he\u2019s not asking you. If Onyx Path doesn\u2019t want to do it, so be it. </div> </div> </div>Please cite him actually asking for anything. It went from a hope (#40, on the 10th) to a direct statement of what Onyx Path needs to do (#48, the 20th, after more updates).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He doesn\u2019t have to like it and he doesn\u2019t need you to tell him how S-O-L he is. I think he knows. </div> </div> </div>No, he doesn't. I don't. You don't. Because we haven't seen the what the errata that didn't make it in is yet. That was my whole point in post #51.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, in post #53 you start to characterize Bamboozle as \u201cdemanding\u201d things. That\u2019s emotionally loading language designed to characterize the speaker. </div> </div> </div>And you've yet to say why it's inaccurate.<br /> <br /> Also... all you're doing is using loaded language to make me look like an asshole so you feel justified in these sorts of posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More importantly, you don\u2019t know why anybody uses Backerkit. </div> </div> </div>I didn't make any comment where that's relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...that it\u2019s his fault for being a Backerkit Pre-order. </div> </div> </div>And you're putting words in my mouth. I never said he was &quot;at fault&quot; for anything. I said that Backerkit pre-order sales don't get the same things as KS backers get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That may be true, but why do you need to be the guy who tells him? </div> </div> </div>I was one of the people talking to him when he said it, so I was the guy that said what I said. Same as you seem to think all of this means you're the one that &quot;needs&quot; to do this song and dance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why are you surprised that someone called you out? </div> </div> </div>Nope. Just as I'm not surprised that I'm being called out with extreme hypocrisy as you toss around the word &quot;judgemental&quot; exactly as you accuse me of using the word &quot;demand.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like I said, I find the shallowness of all this frustrating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He\u2019s not any more demanding than innumerable other people when they ask for stuff. </div> </div> </div>So you're going to damn him with faint praise as well?<br /> <br /> I don't know... I think something like, &quot;Given the situation and likely large amount of errata we'll get, what would it take for OP to get PoD-at-Cost to Backerkit pre-orderers so they can get some relief if they want to get a copy with the errata included?&quot; would be way less of a demand in phrasing.<br /> <br /> Again, there's no &quot;asking&quot; or &quot;request&quot; here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like many people in his situation, he\u2019s afraid the answer will be no, so he makes his case rather earnestly and pulls on strings of feeling cheated and the hope that someone will cut him a break, if only out of good will. </div> </div> </div>... wha?<br /> <br /> Are you trying to say this is a good thing? Or even a justifiable thing? That it's OK for people to justify being manipulative out of fear? I don't think he's doing this at all... I think he's just frustrated, phrased something poorly, and hasn't really said much since that got pointed out to know more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus you\u2019re hung up with him \u2018demanding\u2019 this <i>\u201cright now\u201d</i>. </div> </div> </div>Nobody said &quot;right&quot; now. He said now, I said now. You're adding this to further make me look bad because honestly dealing with what I said apparently wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you\u2019re completely wrong. </div> </div> </div>Then why did you say, &quot;Do I think all Backerkit folks should get backer benefits like POD at-cost printing? No.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, it\u2019s not my company and not my decision. But that\u2019s a weasel answer and I don\u2019t like those, even though I think that\u2019s fair to point out. </div> </div> </div>It not being your company is irrelevant. You're introducing this so you can look good while you say you're not going to 'weasel' by using it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...prestige hard copy. </div> </div> </div>There are no prestige copies. Scion 2e's KS was to fund a traditional print run that will be sold in retail stores, not to get fancy copies like the KS for the WOD, CofD, and Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d let them get POD at-cost as a goodwill gesture. </div> </div> </div>And maybe it'll still happen!<br /> <br /> It's just too early to know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exposition aside, I think he\u2019s got it wrong. I think you\u2019re wrong too. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really feel like you're actually listening to either of us? Hence it feels like there's a disconnect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s been a good thing and he shouldn\u2019t minimize it because this Scion situation is unfortunate. </div> </div> </div>And now you're &quot;characterizing&quot; again. I don't see any minimization of it... he's been working to make sure this never happen again as he keeps using this process. Clearly he cares about using it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And just because we made RPGs without this step for decades, doesn\u2019t mean I want to go backwards. I\u2019m not saying that to Rich, I\u2019m saying it to you. </div> </div> </div>See? This is why you come off as sounding like you think Rich wants to stop it. I never said I want it to stop, I'm just pointing out that it is, in fact,not vital. You're taking that to this place out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t know if you\u2019re being snarky or sincere. </div> </div> </div>Both? I'm completely sincere, but the phrasing is certainly snarky esp. in how it plays off previous wording.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For what it\u2019s worth, I don\u2019t think you\u2019re a bad person. </div> </div> </div>Coulda fooled me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you\u2019re really invested in Onyx Path and you like their writers and developers and you don\u2019t want to see the company hurt. </div> </div> </div>What a very backhandedly polite way of saying, &quot;shut up fanboy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But circumstance has really screwed Bamboozle and it doesn\u2019t have to be his fault that it happened. </div> </div> </div>It screwed over everyone that backed or pre-ordered the books; even if to different extents. It screwed over Neall and Rich too, since it was an accident that's going to negatively impact the game-line going forward even if good improvements come from the error.<br /> <br /> Nobody said it was any of the backer or pre-order folks fault.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Empathy doesn\u2019t have to be disloyalty. </div> </div> </div>Empathy doesn't mean not calling someone out if you think they're saying something in a way that's hurting the cause, or at least their case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I\u2019m wrong and you just like arguing with people, well... my time is just about up here anyway. </div> </div> </div>There are other options for what I am if you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T01:19:28-07:00","id":1307711,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Dial it back. Now.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T15:04:43-07:00","id":1308134,"title":"","content":"Now that the Neall letter has arrived I can say that my fear was really growing on too much. A single page of errata for each book and a FAQ is not too much to use at a game table.<br /> I'm not entirely satisfied of the process and of the apology because I think they could have acknowledged that they should have listen more to the community warnings but the final result is really near what I wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20788-burbankfr","user":"Burbankfr","date":". 04-26-2019, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20788-burbankfr","name":"Burbankfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:05:54-07:00","id":1308159,"title":"","content":"Happy birthday for me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:08:07-07:00","id":1308160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burbankfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1308134#post1308134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that the Neall letter has arrived I can say that my fear was really growing on too much. A single page of errata for each book and a FAQ is not too much to use at a game table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I think the waiting magnified the situation. In hindsight, I also think discussing it through the medium of the MMN without also direct backer communication probably added some tension. Not that utilizing both wouldn\u2019t have been fine.<br /> <br /> That said, it was a good update. A thorough explanation and a sincere apology. Here\u2019s to moving forward!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:34:48-07:00","id":1308168,"title":"","content":"Just as a comment, I did like the FAQ, not that I didn\u2019t understand any of the points Neal put into that, but, it requires some forum time.<br /> <br /> Also, the character sheets side by side: THANK YOU!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:50:03-07:00","id":1308173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1308159#post1308159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happy birthday for me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Many happy returns. \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:54:12-07:00","id":1308174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1308159#post1308159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happy birthday for me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Congrats for the ding!<br /> New level new challenges!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T17:55:30-07:00","id":1308183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burbankfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1308134#post1308134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that the Neall letter has arrived I can say that my fear was really growing on too much. A single page of errata for each book and a FAQ is not too much to use at a game table.</div> </div> </div> </div>For those - like me - that did not found letter from Neall on itself - here it is <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/scion-2nd-edition-tabletop-rpg/posts/2491501\" target=\"_blank\">on Kickstarter page</a> of Scion 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T20:59:55-07:00","id":1308229,"title":"","content":"There are still a few people crapping themselves on the Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> I think they might lose a whole half dozen future backers over this :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T00:58:50-07:00","id":1308253,"title":"","content":"With whole errata and FAQ being one page each - I think that 'damage' is minimal. And I'm glad that we have final versions of PDFs now. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-03-2019, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T06:14:30-07:00","id":1308291,"title":"","content":"This worries me: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">On fixing it, the PDFs and PODs of </span></span></span><b>Scion Second Edition</b><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> will be updated with the errata, corrected sample character sheets, and backer credits</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <br /> My reading of that is that the printed books don't currently include the backer credits. Every backer tier included getting your name in the credits, and yet they're apparently going to be missing from the printed Scion books (Between Kickstarter and Backerkit). I'm not sure you can reasonably claim that this meets the rewards promised.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T10:02:33-07:00","id":1308319,"title":"","content":"Given that the alternative is to go back and reprint the books (which is quite probably prohibitively expensive), I don't see a better compromise. This was an unforseen glitch in the system, not a deliberate oversight. I'm happy to get the books. I don't want OP to suffer financially over an error, and don't see how that would benefit anyone. It won't serve any purpose to keep complaining, either; they already know what happened, and how frustrated people are, and it wasn't deliberate on their part. They have changed procedures going forward, but they can't go back in time to change anything, so all that can reasonably be expected is for them to do damage control (done), keep us in the loop (done), and do thing differently so it doesn't happen again (done).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T10:15:18-07:00","id":1308320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1301777-scion-2e-final-available-for-backers?p=1308319#post1308319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the alternative is to go back and reprint the books (which is quite probably prohibitively expensive), I don't see a better compromise. This was an unforseen glitch in the system, not a deliberate oversight. I'm happy to get the books. I don't want OP to suffer financially over an error, and don't see how that would benefit anyone. It won't serve any purpose to keep complaining, either; they already know what happened, and how frustrated people are, and it wasn't deliberate on their part. They have changed procedures going forward, but they can't go back in time to change anything, so all that can reasonably be expected is for them to do damage control (done), keep us in the loop (done), and do thing differently so it doesn't happen again (done).</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite whatever else maybe taken from my previous post, I agree. A reprint isn\u2019t justified for the actually number of errors, and while backer credits might be \u2018fun\u2019 (I\u2019d rather have the word count for the game personally), I would hope people just drop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T10:41:47-07:00","id":1308326,"title":"","content":"Also, to be technical, the reward only promises that backer names will appear on the credits page under a title based on their pledge level.<br /> <br /> It never even says the credits page will be in the books (though obviously we all assume that to be the case from previous Onyx Path Kickstarters). Since theoretically a credits page on their website would qualify for what was promised (I've backed projects where this is explicitly what they did because there wasn't going to be an effective way to put out a credits list with the product), inclusion in all future PDF and PoD sales certainly does.<br /> <br /> Given the current situation, a reprint isn't going to happen because most people seem fine with the errata and FAQ being as short as they are despite concerns built up by the unknown.<br /> <br /> Individually, if anyone's really unhappy with the final product anyway, they can contact Rich and see about sending it back and getting a refund (I'm not sure Rich can stop it getting sent out now). Otherwise, we get what we get, and people will decide how that influences their future decisions for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T05:50:30-07:00","id":1308653,"title":"","content":"I'd have to check, but I don't think the recent Kickstarters have had the credits pages in the printed books. Which I don't mind. It's a cost addition to each printed book. Put in the PDF version and I'm fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T10:55:03-07:00","id":1308723,"title":"","content":"For the &quot;prestige&quot; or &quot;deluxe&quot; style Kickstarters, Onyx Path is moving towards having the credits section in the fancy copy, and in the PDF (IIRC), but leaving them out of the PoD files. This is pretty explicitly to cut down on printing costs for the future PoDs since most people don't actually want a bunch of pages of people's names ticking the price up.<br /> <br /> There isn't really a standard yet for Kickstarters meant to fund traditional print runs with the intent of getting them into physical distribution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:18:42-07:00","id":1308730,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification. I didn't have a way of checking my books until I got home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:56:42-07:00","id":1308751,"title":"","content":"I would thank the guy if the they forgot to add 20 pages of names of people I don\u2019t know. Not that I don\u2019t like to see my name there (page 195, 3rd from the top on the 4th column), but we are talking about 21 pages in Origin.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on PDF we have all properly there, and the FAQ is nice (not sure we would have it if we didn\u2019t need the Errata).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"k